{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_aaza2felswlmazuwkh6y24pvgjgylruioqh5je4bul4fntmck4hq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The project now builds cleanly with all `unimplemented!()` placeholders replaced by working implementations.\n\nSummary of what I implemented in `src/bigint.rs`:\n\n- **Construction**: `zero()`, `from_int()`, `from_str()`, `copy()` matching the C semantics (including the quirky size-counting in `from_int`).\n- **Conversion/printing**: `to_int()`, `print()`, `Display` (prints all stored digits with the negative sign).\n- **Inspection**: `is_64_bit()` (size < 10), `is_zero()`, `lt_zero()`, `gt_zero()`, `lezero()`, `gezero()`, `abs()`, `is_even()`, `is_odd()`.\n- **Arithmetic**: `add()`/`sub()` with all four sign cases, `mul()` with the 64-bit fast path, `divmod()` using slow subtraction (matching the C algorithm), `div()`, `mod()`, `pow()`, `fast_pow()` with both 64-bit fast path and the recursive halving algorithm, `modinv()` (extended Euclidean).\n- **Other**: `sqrt()` via binary search, `is_prime()` with the early checks (even / divisible by 5 / digit-sum mod 3) plus trial division up to sqrt.\n- **Free functions**: `gt`, `lt`, `ge`, `le`, `delete`, plus traits `Neg`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `PartialOrd`, `Display`.\n\nI added a small `effective_slice()` helper that ignores leading zeros in comparisons, so equality and ordering behave correctly even when the C-style `from_str(\"100\")` produces digits with possible leading zeros. The sanity test exercising factorial(100), fast_pow, modinv, sqrt, prime testing, and 30-digit arithmetic all passed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":146,"cache_read_input_tokens":41344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":146,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"ses